      "body": "## Motivation\n\nGLM-5.2 produces garbled/repetitive output and low MTP acceptance with TP=2, PP=4, NEXTN, and NPU Graph enabled on Ascend 910B4.\n\nThe NPU graph replay path has two PP tensor handling issues:\n- Preplanned verification does not refresh incoming PP tensors in the graph-bound buffers before replay.\n- PP outputs are sliced by request count, truncating token rows when speculative verification uses multiple tokens per request.\n\nFixes #46581\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Copy incoming PP tensors into the existing graph-bound buffers before preplanned replay, preserving buffer addresses and avoiding attention metadata reinitialization.\n- Skip transport markers that do not correspond to graph input buffers.\n- Slice PP outputs to `bs * captured_req_width` to preserve all token rows in the selected graph batch.\n- Add regression tests for repeated replay, in-place buffer updates, transport markers, padded batches, and token widths of 1, 2, and 4.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAdded CPU unit tests with a mocked graph backend in:\n`test/registered/unit/npu/graph_runner/test_npu_graph_runner.py`\n\nRun with:\n\n```bash\npython3 -m pytest test/registered/unit/npu/graph_runner/test_npu_graph_runner.py -v\n```\n\nValidation pending:\n- Unit test execution.\n- End-to-end output correctness and MTP acceptance checks on Ascend 910B4 with the configuration from #46581.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40326718349](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40326718349)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40326718160](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40326718160)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40326718333](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40326718333)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
